# AI CRM Intelligence Platform - Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

## v0.1.0 — Phase 1: Core Database & Infrastructure
Date: March 13, 2026

Complete implementation of the relational database layer, core entity models, and automated migration system.

### Added
* 🐣 Complete database layer using SQLAlchemy 2.0 with full async support.
* 🐣 Core ORM models for the ecosystem: `Company`, `Lead`, `Enrichment`, `GeneratedContent`, and `LLMEval`.
* 🐣 Alembic migration infrastructure with an initial auto-generated schema revision.
* 🐣 Comprehensive Enum types for status tracking, seniority levels, and evaluation categories.
* 🐣 Integration test for verifying database connectivity and async session handling.
* 🐣 Support for `cryptography` to handle MySQL `caching_sha2_password` authentication.

### Changed
* 🔧 Refined database schema for MySQL compatibility, using `CHAR(36)` for UUIDs and `MEDIUMTEXT` for HTML payloads.
* 🔧 Enhanced configuration system with dynamic `.env` file loading and separate sync/async connection strings.
* 🔧 Optimized data retrieval with strategic indexes on industry, email, and timestamp columns.
* 🔧 Updated Docker Compose to align environment variables with application settings.

### Fixed
* 🐛 Resolved circular dependency issues in model relationships using type-checking blocks and forward references.
* 🐛 Standardized database server defaults to align with lowercase Enum definitions.

### Docs
* 📄 Added a visual Database Schema diagram in `docs_resources/`.

### Style
* 🎨 Refined workspace management via updated `.gitignore` and `.geminiignore` patterns.

## v0.0.1 — Phase 0: Project Scaffold & Foundation
Date: March 12, 2026

Initialization of the project structure, dependency management, and core infrastructure.

### Added
* 🐣 Complete directory structure following the implementation plan.
* 🐣 Environment management with `pyproject.toml` and `uv`.
* 🐣 Multi-service Docker infrastructure (MySQL, Redis, Qdrant).
* 🐣 Core configuration module (`pydantic-settings`) and structured logging (`structlog`).
* 🐣 Base exception classes and shared utility skeletons.
